From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] quartz: the Color Space Converter filter (9106)

Wine had no Color Space Converter (CLSID_Colour), the filter Windows' Intelligent
Connect puts between two RGB pins of different depths. OpenCV's DirectShow capture
(videoInput: a Sample Grabber set to RGB24 behind the capture pin) and other
grabber programs failed with VFW_E_CANNOT_CONNECT whenever the source gave RGB32
(a screen capture source, a virtual camera). Converts between RGB32, ARGB32, RGB24,
RGB565, RGB555 and (input only) palettized RGB8, either orientation, honouring the
output stride and dynamic format changes; registered as on Windows: "Color Space
Converter", DirectShow filters category, merit 0x00400001.
---
--- /dev/null
+++ b/dlls/quartz/colour.c
@@ -0,0 +1,596 @@
